  "query_preview": "..\nSYNOPTIC OVERVIEW: \n\nAn omega blocking pattern is causing a digging trough to delay \nits advancement eastward, creating a conveyor belt of moisture \ntransport northward from the desert southwest region. This \nmoisture transport may elevate PoPs, however, increasing clouds in\nour CWA will reduce diurnal heating which should limit precip in \nour region today through Tuesday.\n\nMONDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY NIGHT:\nThe upper-level low, aforementioned above, will transition into a\ncut-off low. An embedded shortwave in the mid-levels may increase\nPoPs into Tuesday, though will remain isolated and confined to the\nfurthest-most southwest of our CWA. Chances of a wetting rain\nremain isolated as well. Subsequent warm, dry, and gusty\nconditions on Tuesday will be cause for fire weather concern.\n\nWEDNESDAY MORNING THROUGH FRIDAY:\nA digging longwave trough in central Canada, coinsiding with the\nsouthern cut off low, aiding to tighten the pressure gradient\nforce. This tight PGF will cause gusty winds in our area.\nFurthermore, a cold front associated with a low pressure system\nwill lift through our region throughout the early morning hours of\nThursday. This will create cooler temperatures in the upper\n50s-mid 60s throughout the region to be shortly replaced by a\ndeveloping high-pressure ridge that will warm our CWA back up on\nFriday. Weak disturbances in the strong winds aloft may bring a\nbrief shower or two but models cannot agree on the timing, thus a\ndry forecast is in place for now.\n\nAgreement between models begins to break down come Friday night, \nbut an oncoming upper-level trough is anticipated to dig over \nMontana sometime between Friday night and Saturday afternoon. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Moderate confidence in chances for showers through Wednesday.\n\n- Low to moderate confidence in FireWx Tuesday afternoon. \n\n- Moderate confidence in partial frost Thursday morning.\n\nFINDLEY",
